TEXT -32 -368 Left 3 ;#84 Ferrite bead in a swept signal path
TEXT -32 -296 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=81C4IfONt3o
TEXT -32 -248 Left 2 ;A ferrite bead in series with a 50 ohm signal path passes low frequencies and absorbs high ones.
TEXT -32 -200 Left 2 ;The sweep covers Alan's 10 kHz to 40 MHz bench sweep and continues to 1 GHz.
TEXT 672 -112 Left 2 ;Bead model, illustrative: LBEAD in parallel with
TEXT 672 -80 Left 2 ;the core loss RCORE, with the winding capacitance
TEXT 672 -48 Left 2 ;CPAR across both. Alan names no part or values.
TEXT 672 16 Left 2 ;RS and RSCOPE are the 50 ohm generator and
TEXT 672 48 Left 2 ;scope input the bead sits between.
TEXT -32 272 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 10k 1G
TEXT -32 320 Left 2 !.meas ac Z_40MEG FIND mag((V(in)-V(out))/I(RSCOPE)) AT=40Meg
TEXT -32 368 Left 2 !.meas ac Z_PEAK MAX mag((V(in)-V(out))/I(RSCOPE))
TEXT -32 416 Left 2 !.meas ac LOSS_40MEG FIND mag(V(out)/0.5) AT=40Meg
TEXT -32 464 Left 2 !.meas ac F_3DB WHEN mag(V(out)/0.5)=0.70711
